{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2182-01-28 19:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this stay. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2182-01-28 19:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi… I’ve been so nauseous and vomiting. I haven’t been able to eat. And the nerve pain—burning, stabbing all over my arms and legs—it’s unbearable. I couldn’t sleep at all."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2182-01-28 19:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m sorry you’re going through that. We saw in your chart you have gastroparesis and diabetic neuropathy. Did you skip your dialysis last night?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2182-01-28 19:08:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I was too sick. I just couldn’t do it. My stomach was so full, and the pain was everywhere."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2182-01-28 19:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We’ll get you started on IV fluids and some anti-nausea meds. Your sodium is low, which could be from not eating or drinking. We’ll watch that closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2182-01-28 19:10:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. But please, can I get something for the nerve pain? I’ve tried gabapentin before—it didn’t help. I just need relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2182-01-28 19:11:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. Because of your kidney disease, some pain meds aren’t safe. But we can try pregabalin, which works for nerve pain and is safer for you. We’ll start it tonight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2182-01-28 19:12:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. And no narcotics, right? I don’t want to break my contract."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2182-01-28 19:13:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Correct. We won’t use narcotics. We’ll focus on safe, effective options for your neuropathy and fibromyalgia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2182-01-29 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood cultures and peritoneal fluid came back negative—no infection. That’s good news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2182-01-29 08:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that’s a relief. I was worried about peritonitis again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2182-01-29 08:17:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We irrigated your peritoneal cavity yesterday to make sure it’s clean. Your PD will continue as planned. How’s the nausea today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2182-01-29 08:18:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little better since the IV fluids. But I still feel full and queasy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2182-01-29 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re keeping you on IV ondansetron for now. We’ll also start erythromycin to help your stomach empty. It’s a motility agent, safe for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2182-01-29 08:21:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that from last time. It helped. But I got dizzy with promethazine—should I avoid that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2182-01-29 08:22:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. You had low blood pressure after it, so we stopped it. We’ll stick with ondansetron, which is safer for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2182-01-30 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your gastric emptying study shows 38% of food still in your stomach after 4 hours. That confirms moderate to severe gastroparesis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2182-01-30 09:01:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So that’s why I feel so full. Will the erythromycin help long-term?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2182-01-30 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It helps short-term. For long-term, GI plans to do an EGD with botox injection after discharge. That can relax the stomach valve and improve emptying."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2182-01-30 09:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds good. What about my pain? The pregabalin helped a little, but I’m still uncomfortable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2182-01-30 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve added nortriptyline at night. It helps with nerve pain and can improve sleep. We started at 25mg, but lowered it to 10mg because you felt groggy in the morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2182-01-30 09:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that was better. I wasn’t so tired. Is it safe with my other meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2182-01-30 09:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but we’ll monitor your EKG. Some of your meds, like nortriptyline and fluoxetine, can affect heart rhythm. We’ll check it regularly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2182-01-31 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You haven’t vomited in over 24 hours—that’s great progress. We’re switching your anti-nausea med to the dissolvable ondansetron tablet, as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2182-01-31 08:31:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t needed it much today. Can I try a small meal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2182-01-31 08:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, start with something light—like broth or applesauce. We’ll watch how you tolerate it. Your constipation is also improving with your usual laxatives."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2182-01-31 08:33:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve been worried about that too. What about my insulin? I haven’t been eating much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2182-01-31 08:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We kept your long-acting insulin the same but reduced your mealtime doses since you’re not eating. We’ll adjust it back as you resume eating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2182-02-01 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs today show your sodium is stable at 130, and kidney function is consistent. Creatinine improved slightly to 4.6."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2182-02-01 09:11:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that good? I know my kidneys aren’t great."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2182-02-01 09:12:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s stable, which is what we want. You’re still on peritoneal dialysis as scheduled. No signs of fluid overload or infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2182-02-01 09:13:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my pain? I’m sleeping better with the nortriptyline."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2182-02-01 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. The pregabalin and nortriptyline together are helping. We stopped gabapentin since it wasn’t working and pregabalin is better for your kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2182-02-02 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve had no nausea for two days and are tolerating soft foods. We’ll stop the IV meds today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2182-02-02 08:46:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s wonderful. Can I go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2182-02-02 08:47:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning for discharge on Friday. You’ll go home with pregabalin and nortriptyline. Keep using ondansetron as needed for nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2182-02-02 08:48:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my domperidone? I brought it from home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2182-02-02 08:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you can continue it. It’s not on the official list because it’s not FDA-approved here, but it’s helping your stomach, so keep taking it as before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2182-02-03 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Last night you walked to the nursing station without issues. Your strength and balance are good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2182-02-03 09:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel much stronger. The pain is manageable now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2182-02-03 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll discontinue the erythromycin tomorrow morning. You don’t need it long-term. Keep up with your home meds for constipation and reflux."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2182-02-03 09:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need another gastric study?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2182-02-03 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not now. The one we did confirmed the diagnosis. The next step is the EGD with botox, which GI will schedule."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2182-02-03 09:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my mental health meds? I’ve been taking them all."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2182-02-03 09:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’re on fluoxetine, clonazepam, and modafinil—all continued as before. They help with mood, anxiety, and fatigue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2182-02-04 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. We’re discharging you today. You’ll go home with services to help with follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2182-02-04 08:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel so much better. No vomiting, and the pain is under control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2182-02-04 08:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Remember to follow up with GI, your nephrologist, and your primary doctor. Keep taking your new meds—pregabalin daily and nortriptyline at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2182-02-04 08:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And get the EKG checks, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2182-02-04 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Your pharmacist recommended regular EKGs due to the combination of medications. Call us if nausea returns or pain worsens."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2182-02-04 08:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2182-02-04 08:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2182-02-04 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before discharge. You’re alert, walking well, and your vitals are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2182-02-04 10:16:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I feel ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2182-02-04 10:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nursing will go over your discharge instructions and meds. Your husband can come up now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2182-02-04 10:18:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2182-02-04 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set. You’re cleared to go home. Rest, follow up, and call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2182-02-04 12:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2182-02-04 12:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’re glad you’re feeling better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2182-02-04 12:33:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Bye."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2182-01-28 18:49:00",
    "admission_end": "2182-02-04 17:50:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for nausea, vomiting, and severe neuropathic pain in the setting of type 1 diabetes, gastroparesis, and end-stage renal disease on peritoneal dialysis. She had not completed her dialysis the night before admission and presented with low sodium and poor oral intake. Workup showed no infection, with negative blood and peritoneal cultures. A gastric emptying study confirmed moderate to severe gastroparesis. She was treated with IV fluids, ondansetron, and erythromycin for gastroparesis, which improved over several days. For neuropathic pain and fibromyalgia, pregabalin was started and nortriptyline added, with gabapentin discontinued. She tolerated a gradual return to oral intake, had no emesis for over 48 hours, and was ambulating independently at discharge. She was discharged home with new prescriptions for pregabalin and nortriptyline, instructions to continue domperidone from her personal supply, and plans for outpatient EGD with botox injection. Regular EKG monitoring was recommended due to QT-prolonging medications.",
    "problems": [
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Type 1 diabetes mellitus with diabetic polyneuropathy",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Fibromyalgia",
      "Hypo-osmolality and hyponatremia",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Constipation, unspecified",
      "Hypotension due to drugs"
    ]
  }
}
